From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:36:06 -0500
Subject: feat: peek over the page, Spaces that loop, the address row's buttons
 in the sidebar, and imports from Chrome, Edge, Brave and Vivaldi

The owner's round of 2026-11-01: GitHub issues 62 and 66, the comment
on issue 45, and a review of the welcome flow's import step.

Peek over the page (peek P20, settings T46; issue 62). "Show a peek:
Over the page", the default, shows a peek inside the pinned tab's
window: a translucent tab-scoped widget over the tab's page
(tabs::TabDialogManager), with the page on a card whose bar has Open in
Split View, Open as Tab and Close. The pinned page wears the window's
scrim and takes no input until the peek closes, and the peek goes and
comes back with its tab. The page is made as a tab's (tab helpers), its
own dialogs show over the card, and Open as Tab moves the same page
into the window through the little window's placing code, now shared
(PromotePeekPage). Escape, Cmd-W and a click beside the card close it;
closing runs "Leave site?". "In a small window" keeps the little window.

Loop around Spaces (spaces B45, settings T44; issue 66): on by default,
the next Space after the last is the first, for the keys, the swipe,
the wheel and moving a tab, and a step round the end slides as the
step goes.

The address in the sidebar, the rest of the row (sidebar Y48, Y49;
toolbar T50, T51; the comment on issue 45). The address row lends its
buttons -- the extensions, the pinned actions, the menu -- to a row
under the sidebar's address while it is gone, the same views, so their
popups anchor there. On Windows the frame leaves its caption buttons
to the sidebar's top row, where they show while the pointer is over
it, so the row goes there too. "Edge that shows a hidden sidebar"
(sidebar Y19, settings T45) is 6, 12 or 24 DIP, 12 by default, and
essentials per row gains Up to 2 (sidebar Y33). The hidden sidebar's
clip is refreshed when its slide ends: a layout run from inside the
end left it on, which hid the edge's shadow.

The import step (import I43-I45, welcome W3). Chrome, Edge, Brave and
Vivaldi join Dia in the Chromium family's table, each with a block of
its own; a running browser is told by its profile lock, since
Stedding's process on Windows is chrome.exe. Chromium's own importer
rows offer only what their source can bring, with search engines and
autofill where it can. Settings and the command bar open the step.

Why: the owner's requests of 2026-11-01 (issues 62 and 66, the comment
on issue 45, the review of the import step).
Removable when: never as features; the tab helpers' friend goes if
Chromium gives a previewed page another way to be a tab's.
